<li><strong>Terminal Condition:</strong> Inspect the terminals for corrosion or any other signs of damage, and clean them if necessary.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>3. Maintain One-Quarter Tank Fuel Level:</strong> For safety reasons, it is recommended to keep the fuel tank at approximately one-quarter full before transporting your motorcycle or two-wheeler. This ensures that the bike can be loaded without any fuel spillage risks and helps prevent fuel from evaporating during transit.</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Fuel Level Check:</strong> Verify that the fuel level is at approximately one-quarter capacity. If necessary, refuel your bike to the recommended level before transport.</li>
<li><strong>Fuel Safety:</strong> Ensure that the fuel tank is securely fastened to prevent any fuel leakage during transportation.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>4. FASTag Management:</strong> In India, the FASTag (Frequent and Secure Toll Application System) is a crucial aspect of motorcycle and two-wheeler transportation. Carefully manage your FASTag to ensure a smooth and hassle-free journey.</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>FASTag Management:</strong> Check that your FASTag is functional and properly mounted on your motorcycle or two-wheeler. If necessary, update your FASTag details, including your contact information and vehicle details.</li>
<li><strong>FASTag Safety:</strong> Securely fasten the FASTag and ensure it doesn't come loose during transportation.</li>
